              "type": "written",
              "text": "German foreign policy must for the foreseeable future pursue three great objectives. First, the solution of the reparations burden in a tolerable manner and the maintenance of peace. Second, the protection of ten million Germans living under foreign rule in ceded territories. Third, the adjustment of our eastern frontiers: the recovery of Danzig and the Polish Corridor, and a revision of the frontier in Upper Silesia. In the background stands the eventual union with German Austria. But the principal thing is the liberation of our soil from foreign military occupation. We must first get the strangler off our throat. For this reason, German diplomacy must at present proceed with finesse and avoid catastrophic military confrontations.",
