                "level": "Level 2 Top / Level 3 Bottom (Contextualised Content)",
                "text": "<p>Source B is useful because it shows urban women gaining voting rights under Article 109 and white-collar jobs as typists and teachers. From my own knowledge, women made up nearly 10% of Reichstag deputies and white-collar jobs grew during Stresemann's recovery. Because Rühle-Gerstel wrote for a Berlin literary journal, she focuses mainly on city women.</p><p>Source C is useful for showing limits to change, pointing out that over four million women worked unpaid on farms and factory women earned two-thirds of male pay. Historically, women earned 33% less than men and married civil servants lost their jobs.</p>",
