                "score": "4 / 16 Marks",
                "level": "Level 1 Top / Level 2 Bottom (Basic Description)",
                "text": "<p>Interpretation 2 argues that the \"New Woman\" was an urban myth because most women stayed in low-paid farm and domestic work and faced conservative backlash. However, Interpretation 1 says women gained real liberation because they won the vote in 1918, entered the Reichstag, and took new white-collar office jobs.</p>",
