          "paragraphs": [
            "<span class=\"para-ref\">[3.1]</span> In summer 1920, Hitler directed an aggressive **NSDAP party rebranding**, renaming the organization the National Socialist German Workers' Party to broaden its working-class appeal. Recognizing the necessity of striking visual theater, he adopted the black hooked **swastika party emblem**, angled inside a white circle upon a red field. The design cleverly co-opted imperial colors while deliberately provoking left-wing socialist rivals across Munich.",
            "<span class=\"para-ref\">[3.2]</span> In December 1920, wealthy nationalist donors helped the party purchase the **Völkischer Beobachter newspaper**, giving Hitler an influential print mouthpiece to circulate anti-republican propaganda and racial conspiracy theories. Armed with distinctive paramilitary insignia, printed party newspapers, and regular beer hall rallies drawing thousands of paying spectators, Hitler established himself as the party’s indispensable and dominant public figure."
          ],
