          "paragraphs": [
            "<span class=\"para-ref\">[1.1]</span> In November 1923, amidst national fury over the Ruhr occupation and runaway hyperinflation, Hitler plotted to seize power. Convinced the Weimar Republic was collapsing, he sought to emulate Mussolini’s 1922 March on Rome by launching a coup from Munich. To gain military legitimacy, Hitler enlisted prestigious First World War commander **General Erich Ludendorff** to lead a march against Berlin.",
            "<span class=\"para-ref\">[1.2]</span> On 8 November 1923, Hitler and six hundred armed SA stormtroopers stormed the **Bürgerbräukeller Beer Hall**, interrupting a speech by Bavarian commissioner Gustav von Kahr. Firing a pistol into the ceiling, Hitler declared a national revolution and coerced Bavarian leaders at gunpoint. However, the resulting **failed Munich march (16 dead)** through the streets was met by armed police gunfire, crushing the coup."
          ]
