          "paragraphs": [
            "<span class=\"para-ref\">[2.1]</span> In February 1924, Hitler and fellow putsch conspirators faced trial for high treason in Munich. Rather than denying the charges, Hitler turned the sensational **Munich treason trial** into a national propaganda platform. Sympathetic right-wing judges granted him unrestricted speaking time to attack the Weimar democracy, broadcast nationalist grievances, and justify his armed putsch as patriotic duty before reporters from across Germany.",
            "<span class=\"para-ref\">[2.2]</span> Capitalizing on widespread media coverage, masterly **Hitler courtroom propaganda** transformed him from an obscure regional agitator into a recognized national martyr. Conservative judges showed extraordinary judicial bias, giving him a remarkably **lenient five-year sentence** with immediate parole eligibility. While ordinary treason carried life imprisonment, Hitler served barely nine months in comfortable conditions at Landsberg Fortress, free to receive visitors and plan his political resurgence."
          ],
          "image": "/images/munich_putsch_defendants.jpg",
