          "Source A": "Published in Punch on 8 February 1933, days after Adolf Hitler was appointed Reich Chancellor. Vice-Chancellor Franz von Papen and 85-year-old President Paul von Hindenburg are depicted reluctantly hoisting Hitler onto their shoulders while cheering SA stormtroopers march past. Hinge Question: Why did conservative aristocrats like Franz von Papen believe they could safely \"carry\" Hitler into power without being overthrown by him?",
