          "act_title": "Stage 4: The Backstairs Plot & Hindenburg’s Capitulation",
          "paragraphs": [
            "<span class=\"para-ref\">[4.1]</span> Throughout late January 1933, aggressive **von Papen backroom intrigue** operated behind closed doors in the presidential palace. Papen allied with the President’s influential son, Oskar von Hindenburg, and state secretary Otto Meissner. Together, they relentlessly lobbied the eighty-five-year-old Field Marshal, successfully securing the crucial **Hindenburg appointment persuaded** by arguing that an alliance with Hitler was the only alternative to military dictatorship or civil war.",
            "<span class=\"para-ref\">[4.2]</span> Crucially, Papen eased Hindenburg’s lingering reservations by promoting the complacent **'Hitler boxed in' belief**. Papen foolishly boasted that within two months Hitler would be squeezed into a corner, noting that only three of eleven cabinet ministers were Nazis, while Papen retained the right to attend all meetings with Hindenburg. The traditional conservative elite foolishly believed they had safely harnessed Hitler to serve their own nationalist agenda."
          ],
