          "act_title": "Stage 2: Radio (Volksempfänger) & The Daily Press",
          "paragraphs": [
            "<span class=\"para-ref\">[2.1]</span> Goebbels recognized radio as the ultimate instrument for modern mass indoctrination. In 1933, the state sponsored the **Volksempfänger cheap radio**, mass-producing sets priced at just seventy-six marks so ordinary German working families could afford them. The radios were engineered with limited reception capabilities, successfully preventing listeners from picking up foreign news broadcasts while piping Hitler’s major speeches directly into living rooms.",
            "<span class=\"para-ref\">[2.2]</span> By 1939, rapid distribution achieved over **70% household radio ownership**, representing the highest rate of radio access anywhere in Europe. The regime backed this broadcast monopoly with strict **foreign broadcast bans**, making listening to foreign radio stations a criminal offense punishable by penal imprisonment, while municipal loudspeakers in factories and cafes broadcast Nazi propaganda to captive public audiences."
          ],
