            "content": "Report of the Secret State Police (Gestapo), Station Düsseldorf-South, 14 May 1936:\nSubject: Citizen Friedrich K., grocer, resident at Kölner Straße 42.\nComplaint: An anonymous report was lodged by Frau B., neighbour of the accused. The informant states that during the celebration of the Führer’s birthday on 20 April, the suspect failed to display the national swastika banner. Furthermore, in his shop he reportedly uttered to customers: \"The brown bigwigs live off butter and meat while we must make sacrifices for the Four-Year Plan.\"\nAction Taken: The accused was brought in for interrogation. He admitted making careless remarks regarding food rationing. In view of subversive defeatism, he has been taken into protective custody (Schutzhaft) and transferred to Esterwegen concentration camp for ideological re-education."
