          "caption": "National Socialist Women’s League (NS-Frauenschaft) Assembly, Sigmaringen (mid-1930s): Beneath swastika banners and the central Lebensrune ('life rune') emblem, local organisers lectured millions of German women on domestic thrift, infant care, and the regime's anti-feminist doctrine of Kinder, Küche, Kirche."
