          "paragraphs": [
            "<span class=\"para-ref\">[3.1]</span> To glorify prolific motherhood, the regime established prestigious national honours for fertile women. In 1938, Hitler instituted **Mother's Cross medals**, awarded annually on his mother's birthday. Medals were graded into bronze for four children, silver for six, and the revered **gold cross (8 children)** or more. Recipients received public salutes from the Hitler Youth, preferential shopping queues, and seats of honour at state ceremonies.",
            "<span class=\"para-ref\">[3.2]</span> Beyond conventional family units, Heinrich Himmler's SS founded the secretive **Lebensborn maternity program** in 1935. Initially established to provide confidential maternity homes for unmarried women of pure Nordic ancestry, Lebensborn evolved into a selective breeding experiment. Unmarried Aryan women were actively encouraged to mate with SS officers in state clinics to produce genetically pure children, prioritizing demographic expansion over traditional Christian moral values."
          ],
