            "<span class=\"para-ref\">[2.1]</span> To combat massive youth unemployment and foster national solidarity, the regime established the **Reich Labour Service (RAD)** under Konstantin Hierl. Converted into a compulsory state program in July 1935, the law mandated **six months compulsory labour** for all unmarried young men aged eighteen to twenty-five prior to their military conscription, removing hundreds of thousands of men from unemployment figures.",
